   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "M3.4: the MIDI Viewer (piano roll + basic synth).\n\nInput: m5_duo_cc.mid (copied into input/ by the workflow runner; otherwise copy it from custom_nodes/com5fy/workflows/inputs/). Clarinet + piano, 100 BPM in 3/4, 75 BPM from bar 3, 4/4 from bar 4; the clarinet's 4th note (A4) is bent up a quarter tone; the piano holds the sustain pedal in bar 2.\n\nPress Run. Look at:\n1. MIDI Viewer (top): one row per key (keyboard on the left, C's labelled), Clarinet in blue, Piano in orange, barlines with measure numbers 1-4 (bars get longer at bar 3 (slower tempo) and bar 4 (4/4)), faint beat lines. The clarinet's A4 sits half a row above A4 (+50 cents). Softer notes are fainter (piano vel 64 vs clarinet 90).\n2. Hover a note: pitch (+ cents), MIDI number, velocity, track, channel, start and length.\n3. Press play: the basic synth (one soft tone for every track). The playhead moves; sounding notes get a white outline. Click or drag on the roll to jump. Listen for the quarter-tone A4 and the piano chord in bar 2 held by the pedal until bar 3.\n4. zoom: 1 fits the whole file; raise it (e.g. 4) and scroll sideways (wheel / trackpad / scrollbar); the view follows the playhead while playing. It redraws without running again.\n5. MIDI to Audio (basic synth) -> Audio Playback: the same rendering as an AUDIO output (waveform, spectrogram), to save or feed other nodes.\n6. Bottom row: the M2.1 duo score -> Sequence -> MIDI -> MIDI Viewer: flute + clarinet with velocities from the dynamics, and the flute's quarter-flat drawn between rows (it plays on its own channel, bent).\n\nTry: your own .mid files (put them in input/ and press R); a drum track (channel 10 plays noise hits)."
   ],
